`RESULT.md` is on `main`, and it matches the copy I wrote byte for byte. The commit that added it is `a33db81` ("Add files via upload," by evan ketchum). I didn't make or push that commit.

The raw transcript and manifest were on my machine but not in the repo, so the links were dead. I've now copied them into the clone and checked them against the manifest. All four listed files verify as OK: `gpg_verify_raw_status.txt`, `input_sha256.txt`, `key_fingerprint.txt`, and `repo_head.txt`.

I haven't committed or pushed anything, since this sandbox has no GitHub credentials. The four files are untracked in `/home/user/kcn-baseline-evidence`. To publish them from your machine, run:

```
