git add MANIFEST.sha256 gpg_verify_raw_status.txt input_sha256.txt key_fingerprint.txt repo_head.txt
git commit -m "Add raw GPG verify transcript and manifest for BTP-001 result record"
git push origin main
```



Or upload the same five files through the GitHub web UI, as the earlier commit was done. Either way, leave `RESULT.md` and the signed sign-off untouched.

The manifest covers the four evidence files but not `RESULT.md`, which is fine because `RESULT.md` is already on `main` and its hash is `8ba5508a…0253`. If you want it covered, I can add it to the manifest in a new commit.
